{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,2]],"date-time":"2026-11-02T12:33:58Z","timestamp":1793622838192,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":41,"publisher":"Optica Publishing Group","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,22]],"date-time":"2024-02-22T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1708560000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1364\/OA_License_v2#VOR-OA"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,22]],"date-time":"2024-02-22T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1708560000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/opg.optica.org\/policies\/opg-tdm-policy.json"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100021856","name":"Ministero dell'Universit\u00e0 e della\n\t\t\t\t\t\tRicerca","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["PRIN 2022 CUP: D53D23002850006"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["PRIN 2022 CUP: D53D23002850006"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100021856","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000780","name":"European Commission","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["Next Generation EU: PE0000023-NQSTI"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["Next Generation EU: PE0000023-NQSTI"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000780","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100003981","name":"Agenzia Spaziale Italiana","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["2023-13-HH.0"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2023-13-HH.0"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100003981","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100003981","name":"Agenzia Spaziale Italiana","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["MOST"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["MOST"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100003981","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["opg.optica.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Optica Quantum"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,25]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>\n                    Interferometric methods have been recently investigated to achieve\n\t\t\t\t\tsub-Rayleigh imaging and precision measurements of faint incoherent\n\t\t\t\t\tsources up to the ultimate quantum limit. Here we consider\n\t\t\t\t\tsingle-photon imaging of two point-like emitters of unequal intensity.\n\t\t\t\t\tThis is motivated by the fact that pairs of natural emitters typically\n\t\t\t\t\thave unequal brightness, for example, binary star systems and\n\t\t\t\t\texoplanets. We address the problem of estimating the transverse\n\t\t\t\t\tseparation\n                    <jats:italic toggle=\"yes\">d<\/jats:italic>\n                    or the relative intensity . Our theoretical analysis shows that\n\t\t\t\t\tthe associated statistical errors are qualitatively different from the\n\t\t\t\t\tcase of equal intensity. We employ multi-plane light conversion\n\t\t\t\t\ttechnology to implement Hermite\u2013Gaussian (HG) spatial-mode\n\t\t\t\t\tdemultiplexing (SPADE), and demonstrate sub-Rayleigh measurement of\n\t\t\t\t\ttwo emitters with a Gaussian point-spread function. The experimental\n\t\t\t\t\terrors are comparable with the theoretical bounds. The latter are\n\t\t\t\t\tbenchmarked against direct imaging, yielding an  improvement in the signal-to-noise\n\t\t\t\t\tratio, which may be significant when the primary source is much\n\t\t\t\t\tbrighter than the secondary one, for example, as for imaging of\n\t\t\t\t\texoplanets.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1364\/opticaq.505457","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,26]],"date-time":"2024-01-26T09:00:13Z","timestamp":1706259613000},"page":"46","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1364\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":35,"title":["Single-photon sub-Rayleigh precision measurements of a pair of incoherent sources of unequal intensity"],"prefix":"10.1364","volume":"2","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0898-3569","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Luigi","family":"Santamaria","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Matera Space Center"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0924-0698","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Fabrizio","family":"Sgobba","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Matera Space Center"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5227-4009","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Cosmo","family":"Lupo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/034zgem50","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"name":"INFN"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"285","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,22]]},"reference":[{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"261","DOI":"10.1080\/14786447908639684","volume":"8","author":"Rayleigh","year":"1879","journal-title":"Lond. Edinb. Dublin philos. Mag. J. Sci."},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R2","author":"Goodman","year":"2008"},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"780","DOI":"10.1364\/OL.19.000780","volume":"19","author":"Hell","year":"1994","journal-title":"Opt. Lett."},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R4","author":"Kolobov","year":"2007"},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"2733","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.85.2733","volume":"85","author":"Boto","year":"2000","journal-title":"Phys. Rev.\n\t\t\t\t\tLett."},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"013827","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevA.79.013827","volume":"79","author":"Giovannetti","year":"2009","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. A"},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R7","author":"Helstrom","year":"1976"},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R8","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"031033","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevX.6.031033","volume":"6","author":"Tsang","year":"2016","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. X"},{"key":"opticaq-2-1-46-R9","doi-asserted-by":"publisher